As always hungry Wolf was roaming around. For the whole week he had nothing for dinner. Suddenly wind brought him smell of fish from the trail. Wolf liked meat much more, but now he was even ready to graze if grass would grow already. Taking in the air, Wolf cautiously prowled to the trail and his heart joyfully began to beat expecting double prey. His first intention was to attack poor woman  immediately but life in the forest made him cautious, so the beast didn't hurry sliding slowly after his victim. Moreover, she could lead him to even larger prey. Saliva was dripping off his fangs and stomach was monotonously whining.